  "theory": {
    "intro": "Dotting a vector with itself gives the square of its length. That link turns a length question into a dot product question, and it lets you expand brackets such as $|\\underset{\\sim}{a}+\\underset{\\sim}{b}|^{2}$.",
    "facts": [
      "$\\underset{\\sim}{a}\\cdot\\underset{\\sim}{a}=|\\underset{\\sim}{a}|^{2}$, because a vector makes an angle of $0^{\\circ}$ with itself.",
      "Rearranged, this gives $|\\underset{\\sim}{a}|=\\sqrt{\\underset{\\sim}{a}\\cdot\\underset{\\sim}{a}}$.",
      "In components it is the usual length rule: $\\underset{\\sim}{a}\\cdot\\underset{\\sim}{a}=a_{1}^{2}+a_{2}^{2}$.",
      "Dot products expand like brackets, so $|\\underset{\\sim}{a}+\\underset{\\sim}{b}|^{2}=|\\underset{\\sim}{a}|^{2}+2\\underset{\\sim}{a}\\cdot\\underset{\\sim}{b}+|\\underset{\\sim}{b}|^{2}$.",
      "Changing the sign changes only the middle term: $|\\underset{\\sim}{a}-\\underset{\\sim}{b}|^{2}=|\\underset{\\sim}{a}|^{2}-2\\underset{\\sim}{a}\\cdot\\underset{\\sim}{b}+|\\underset{\\sim}{b}|^{2}$.",
      "The cross term $2\\underset{\\sim}{a}\\cdot\\underset{\\sim}{b}$ is zero only when the two vectors are perpendicular.",
      "Lengths do not simply add, so $|\\underset{\\sim}{a}+\\underset{\\sim}{b}|\\ne|\\underset{\\sim}{a}|+|\\underset{\\sim}{b}|$ in general."
    ],
    "steps": [
      "Expand the brackets, using $\\underset{\\sim}{a}\\cdot\\underset{\\sim}{b}=\\underset{\\sim}{b}\\cdot\\underset{\\sim}{a}$",
      "Replace each self dot product with a squared magnitude",
      "Substitute the known values and evaluate"
    ]
  },
